@startuml donor-first-deployment
!theme plain
title Remote worker on a donor machine, first deployment (revision 3; variant B shown, see CIP-0009 D0 for A and C): one invitation, one command, nothing to configure; two OS identities; three role-separated keys owned by the bridge identity; the posture is locked by the donor (the machine's owner)

actor "Donor (the machine's owner)" as ADM
participant "curator remote-worker init\n(donor install)" as C
participant "swarma-user-manager\n(sudoers: this absolute path only;\nclosed schema; journal + rollback)" as PH
participant "Bridge identity\nswarma-bridge-<project>\n(keys, config, audit)" as B
participant "Harness identity\nworker-<project>\n(managed home, scratch)" as U
database "DNS (DNSSEC, default)\nTXT _swarma, TXT _swarma-ssh-ca, TLSA\n(validated inside the client)" as DNS
participant "Join point\n(our host, HTTPS: challenge, cert, collect)" as JP
actor "Operator (our side)\nor orchestrator with onboard grant" as OP
participant "Trust registry + key keeper\n(our host)" as T

== 1. invitation ==
OP -> ADM: swarma-invitation/1 {invitation_id, join point, root fingerprint,\nSSH host CA fingerprint, project, role, expires, one-use random code}\nthrough the channel the donor found us by: marketplace deal thread, e-mail, our site\n(the code is a short-lived bootstrap secret; without an invitation: init <domain>, an open application)

== 2. local provisioning (transactional) ==
ADM -> C: curator remote-worker init <invitation>
C -> C: refuse unsupported host; verify the release manifest of /opt/swarma/<release>
C -> PH: create-worker <label>: two accounts (allocated UIDs), homes,\negress anchor by UID, Seatbelt profile (read boundary), launchd daemon unit
PH --> C: journal entry per step (rollback on failure)
C -> B: generate K_sig (Ed25519), K_enc (X25519), K_ssh (Ed25519); 0600, bridge-owned
B -> B: enrolment certificate {K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh, name, role, invitation_id, expires}\nself-signed by K_sig; fingerprint = SHA-256(certificate)
C --> ADM: show fingerprint F

== 3. join (see join-handshake for the transcript) ==
C -> JP: POST /join/challenge {invitation_id}
JP --> C: server challenge (bound to the invitation, 5 min, attempt counter)
C -> DNS: TXT _swarma, TXT _swarma-ssh-ca, TLSA (system resolver; DNS-over-HTTPS when the network strips DNSSEC);\nsignatures validated in the client from the embedded root trust anchor
alt secure and equal to the invitation
  C -> C: record "dns: secure, matches"
else bogus
  C --> ADM: refused{dns_bogus}
else indeterminate (even over DNS-over-HTTPS)
  C --> ADM: refused{dns_unverifiable}: explain; no downgrade
end
C -> JP: POST /join/cert {swarma-join/1 transcript, sig_K_sig, code}\n(HTTPS: Web PKI for the domain, pinned by the TLSA record)
JP -> JP: code (constant time), signature, challenge, expiry;\nconsume invitation atomically (tombstone); rate limit
JP -> OP: pending enrolment: fingerprint F, name, role
OP -> OP: check the enrolment: the key in the donor's signed marketplace card when there is one,\notherwise the invitation the code binds (no voice check)
alt rejected
  OP -> JP: reject
  JP --> C: refused
else admitted
  OP -> T: pin K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh; root-signed admission "K admitted with role R";\ngrants: post to worker thread, read own mailbox, no delegation, expiry
  OP -> OP: swarma-credential-package/1 {root pubkey, operator cert (root-signed), host,\nSSH host CA key, workplace user, binding digest, qualified tuple, policy generation, expiry}\nAEAD to K_enc (X25519 + HKDF + ChaCha20-Poly1305), AAD = transcript digest, signed by the operator cert
  OP -> JP: package ready for <invitation_id>
  C -> JP: POST /join/collect {invitation_id, sig_K_sig(second challenge)}
  JP --> C: package
  C -> B: decrypt with K_enc; verify operator cert against the pinned root;\nverify package signature and AAD
  C -> B: write LOCKED machine config: tool_posture=lockdown, permissions=remote-auto (pair),\npolicy_generation, mcp_package_allowlist=[canonical source of swarma-remote-tools],\npassable_env_names=[], qualified tuple, binding, sandbox revision
  C -> U: install the relay declaration into profile remote-worker (absolute command path)
  C --> ADM: registered; waiting for tasks (status, stop, leave, purge available)
end

== 4. workplace on our host ==
OP -> T: provision workplace for K (dispatcher, grant user.create): OS user,\nTrustedUserCAKeys: short user certificates for K_ssh (principal = workplace user), restrict + command="/opt/swarma/libexec/swarma-rb-exec",\nsshd Match: no forwarding, no PTY, no user rc/env; egress by UID
note right of T: see remote-worker-turn for the connection
@enduml
